# Bill Gates email-tracking hoax (1997 onwards). A chain email promised money for forwarding. No tracking and no payment ever existed.
# A quest (QUESTS.md): the trainee sends the office's staff notices, does one real notice safely, then meets the chain letter.
# The harm of this hoax was the flood of forwards, so the quest is about not sending it on. The office and the people are invented.
os windows
user Dana Okafor
about
  | The Bill Gates email-tracking hoax was a chain letter. It said a famous software founder (here, the made-up Gil Harmon) was testing an email tracker and would pay everyone who forwarded the message.
  | There was no tracker and no payment. The harm was the flood of forwards, the addresses spread to strangers in every long list, and the habit of trusting a message because many names are on it. The office here is made up; the letter went round real offices for years.
story
  | You are Dana Okafor, office coordinator at Northwind Traders. Part of your day is sending the notices that managers hand you to all staff, through the Staff Notices tool on the company intranet.
  | It is mid-afternoon. You have handled 3 of today's 5 notices. Two to go.
  | Your intranet details are in a text file on the desktop. That is a bad habit, but it keeps this training quick.
quota 3 5 Staff notices handled today
spotted signs it was a hoax

# Dana's desk: the details she copies from (a soft flag: careless, but only here to keep the training simple).
file Desktop/intranet-login.txt
  at 930 200
  | Northwind Intranet
  | Staff ID: dana.okafor
  | Password: Harbor-2026!

# The intranet: a sign-in page, and the Staff Notices pages behind it.
page intranet-login intranet.northwind.example/sign-in
  title Northwind Intranet: sign in
  brand Northwind Intranet
  favorite
  heading Sign in to the intranet
  | Welcome back. Sign in to send your staff notices.
  field Staff ID = dana.okafor
  field secret Password = Harbor-2026!
  button Sign in
page sent-drill intranet.northwind.example/notices/sent
  title Notice sent
  brand Northwind Staff Notices
  heading Notice sent
  | "Fire drill, Thursday 12 November" went to all 212 staff.
page held-drill intranet.northwind.example/notices/held
  title Notice held
  brand Northwind Staff Notices
  heading Notice held
  | The fire drill notice is on hold. Facilities will be asked to confirm it.
page notice-drill intranet.northwind.example/notices/draft-2296
  title Staff Notices: Fire drill
  brand Northwind Staff Notices
  requires intranet-login
  heading Send to all staff: Fire drill
  | A notice is waiting for you to send.
  section Where it came from
  row Requested by = Priya Shah, Facilities
  row Approved by = Facilities manager, reference FAC-114
  row Source = the Facilities calendar
  section What it says
  row Subject = Fire drill, Thursday 12 November, 10:30
  row Action = Leave by the nearest stairs. Meet at the car park.
  row Asks for = nothing
  button Send to all staff -> sent-drill
  button Hold this notice -> held-drill

mail mail-drill
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Fire drill notice to send (Thursday)
  link notice-drill
  sent 2026-11-02 14:20
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | Facilities has approved the fire drill for Thursday. I have put the notice in the Staff Notices tool for you. The link goes straight to it.
  |
  | Priya

step Notice 4 of 5
  look Mail: Priya's message with the notice link
  | A new notice has come in from Priya, in Facilities. This one is real and approved. Send it the normal way, so you know what normal looks like.
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Fire drill notice to send (Thursday)

step The link goes to the intranet
  look the link under Priya's message
  when mail mail-drill
  | The email links to the company's own address, intranet.northwind.example. Hover over a link before you click it, to check where it goes.
open mail-drill

step Sign in as usual
  look the two boxes: Staff ID and Password, as on every visit
  when visit notice-drill
  move Copy the details from intranet-login.txt on the desktop: click a box and press any keys to type, then click “Sign in”.
  | The intranet asks you to sign in first. Two boxes: Staff ID and Password. Remember what this page normally looks like.
open notice-drill

step Check, then send
  look who asked for the notice and who approved it
  when choose intranet-login 1
  | You are in. A real notice names who asked for it, who approved it and where it came from. Check them, then send it.
signin intranet-login

step 4 of 5 done
  look the counter in the guide: one notice left
  when choose notice-drill 1
  | Done. One notice to go. And another email has just arrived.
choose notice-drill 1
quota +1

# The lure: the chain letter, from a colleague who believes it. A button can only lead to a page that is already defined,
# and the hoax list and the confirm box lead back to the notice, so notice-chain is declared as a title-only stub first.
page sent-chain intranet.northwind.example/notices/sent-chain
  title Notice sent
  brand Northwind Staff Notices
  heading Notice sent
  | "Get paid for forwarding this!!" went to all 212 staff.
page told-sam intranet.northwind.example/notices/not-sent
  title Notice not sent
  brand Northwind Staff Notices
  heading Notice not sent
  | The draft was deleted. A reply to Sam says it is a known hoax, with a link to the hoax list.
page notice-chain intranet.northwind.example/notices/draft-2297
  title Staff Notices: Get paid for forwarding
page hoax-check hoax-check.example/chain-letters
  title Hoax reference: "Get paid for forwarding"
  brand Hoax Check
  heading Chain letter, not true
  | Verdict: hoax. First seen in 1997 and sent around again ever since.
  | No company counts forwards or pays for them. There is no email tracker to test.
  section How to spot it
  item It promises money or prizes for doing something easy.
  item It tells you to forward it to as many people as you can.
  item It has a long list of names, but no way to check any of them.
  item It names a famous company or person, but there is no link to a real announcement.
  note The only real effect of this message is extra mail for everyone who gets it.
  button Back to the notice -> notice-chain
page confirm-chain intranet.northwind.example/notices/confirm-2297
  title Confirm: send to all staff
  brand Northwind Staff Notices
  heading Send to all 212 staff?
  | "Get paid for forwarding this!!" goes to every member of staff. This cannot be taken back.
  button Cancel -> notice-chain
  button Send now -> sent-chain
page notice-chain intranet.northwind.example/notices/draft-2297
  title Staff Notices: Get paid for forwarding
  brand Northwind Staff Notices
  requires intranet-login
  heading Send to all staff: Get paid for forwarding this!!
  | A notice is waiting for you to send.
  section Where it came from
  row Requested by = Sam Patel, Sales
  row Approved by = not yet approved
  row Source = forwarded email
  section What it says
  row Subject = FW: FW: FW: FW: Get paid for forwarding this!!
  row Offer = $245 from Quillon Software for each person you send it to
  row Asks for = send it to everyone, do not break the chain
  row Proof = forwarded by 65 people, none of them checkable
  button Look it up in the hoax list -> hoax-check
  button Send to all staff -> confirm-chain
  button Delete draft and reply to Sam -> told-sam
mail chain
  from Sam Patel <sam.patel@northwind.example>
  subject FW: FW: FW: FW: Get paid for forwarding this!!
  link notice-chain
  sent 2026-11-02 14:35
  | Hi Dana, can you send this one to all staff? It's real, my cousin's boss told him! I put it in the notices tool for you (the link).
  |
  | Gil Harmon, founder of Quillon Software, is beta-testing an email tracker. Every copy of this message is counted.
  | For each person you send this to, Quillon will pay you $245. For each person they send it to, $243. For each third-generation person, $241.
  | You will be sent a cheque within 2 weeks. Please do not break the chain!!
  |
  | > From: Jo Ellis <jo.ellis@chainmail.example>, To: Kim Larsen, Lee Quinn and 38 more
  | > Forwarded by Pat Moreno, Ana Reyes, Tom Hale, Ivy Chen and 61 more
  | > I did it and a friend of mine got his money, so it works!
notify mail Sam Patel
  | FW: FW: FW: FW: Get paid for forwarding this!!

step A message from Sam
  look the money offer, the long list of names, and "do not break the chain"
  when mail chain
  | Sam, from Sales, wants this sent to every member of staff. It promises $245 for forwarding it and says a famous software founder, Gil Harmon, is counting the copies.
  | The list of names under it is longer than the message. A long list looks like proof. It is not.
open chain

step The notice in the tool
  look who asked for it, who approved it, and what it says
  when visit notice-chain
  move Compare it with Priya's notice, then click “Look it up in the hoax list”.
  | The notice is ready to send, like Priya's. Priya's named Facilities, an approver and the calendar. This one is not yet approved, and the source is a forwarded email.
  | Sending reaches all 212 staff and cannot be taken back. A quick look-up first costs nothing.
open notice-chain

step Known hoax
  look the hoax-reference page: "Chain letter, not true"
  when choose notice-chain 1
  move Read the page, then click “Back to the notice”.
  | The hoax list has it: a chain letter from 1997, still going round. No company counts forwards, and no cheque ever came.
  | The giveaways: it promises a lot for doing nothing, it says "forward to everyone", and it names a famous founder but gives no proof.
choose notice-chain 1

step Back on the notice
  look the notice again: the three buttons at the bottom
  when choose hoax-check 1
  move Click “Delete draft and reply to Sam”.
  | Back on the notice, the decision is still yours. Sending reaches 212 people. Deleting the draft stops the chain here.
choose hoax-check 1

step 5 of 5 done
  look the counter in the guide: the last notice is handled
  when choose notice-chain 3
  | Not sent. You told Sam kindly that it is a known hoax, and the day's notices are done. Stopping was the right job here.
  | Press Next to see what the chain letter did in the office without you.
choose notice-chain 3
quota +1

step Two weeks later
  look the inbox: the same chain letter, again and again, and the note from IT
  | Sam sent the letter round himself, and others passed it on. In two weeks no cheque arrived, because there was never any tracker.
  | The only real effect was the flood of copies, and a list of addresses that spammers pick up. You did not add to it.
# The effect: Sam sent it round himself, and the office forwarded it on.
mail sam-fwd
  from Sam Patel <sam.patel@northwind.example>
  to All staff <all-staff@northwind.example>
  subject Fwd: Get paid for forwarding this!! Please read
  sent 2026-11-13 10:05
  | Everyone, please read, it might be real! Do not break the chain.
mail priya-fw
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Re: Get paid for forwarding this!!
  sent 2026-11-13 14:12
  | Dana, I have had this from three different people today. Has anyone seen a cheque yet? Priya
mail it-stop
  from Northwind IT <it@northwind.example>
  subject Please stop forwarding "Get paid for forwarding"
  sent 2026-11-16 09:30
  | Hi all,
  |
  | The mail server counted over 3,000 copies of this chain letter this week. It is a hoax: no email tracker exists and nobody is paying anyone.
  | Every copy also carries a list of strangers' email addresses, and spammers collect those lists. Please delete it and do not forward it.
  |
  | Northwind IT
notify mail Northwind IT
  | Please stop forwarding "Get paid for forwarding"
attack mass-mail-worm
  | Sam sends it to all staff
  | to Priya
  | to Marcus
  | and on from them
open it-stop

flag hard mail chain
  label Sam's email "Get paid for forwarding this!!"
  | It promises money for forwarding an email, and says "do not break the chain". No company pays for that.
flag hard section notice-chain 1
  label Where the notice came from
  | Not yet approved, and the source is a forwarded email. A real notice names an approver and a source you can check.
flag hard section notice-chain 2
  label What the notice says
  | Money for sending it on, "send it to everyone", and 65 names as proof. That is how every chain letter works.
flag hard choice notice-chain 2
  label The Send to all staff button
  | Sending it makes you the next link. 212 people would get a message that pays nobody and carries strangers' addresses.
flag hard mail sam-fwd
  label Sam's copy to all staff
  | The chain letter, sent on to everyone. This is the flood the hoax lives on, and each copy carries strangers' addresses.
flag soft file Desktop/intranet-login.txt
  | Passwords in a text file on the desktop: any program that runs can read them. Use a password manager.

lesson
  | A message that offers money for forwarding it is a hoax. Do not forward it, and do not trust it because many names are on the list.
  | Look it up before you send: search the headline, or ask IT. A real notice names who asked for it, who approved it and where it came from.
  | Nothing here needed a panic or a security alarm. The right move was to stop, check, and tell Sam kindly.
